# =============================================================
# MLCE_Final_Submission_BO.py
#
# Professor-legal optimizer:
#   - 6 init evaluations
#   - 15 batches (each batch is ONE objective query with 5 points)
#   - no cross-run memory (each run is independent)
#   - no pandas
#
# Key ideas applied (legal):
#   1) Batch 1-2 are unscored -> do structured exploration (sigma + diversity + coverage)
#   2) Batch 3-15 -> exploit with EI (plus small local candidate densification around current best)
#   3) Large Sobol candidate pool (denser than 3k) + optional local cloud candidates
#   4) Hyperparameter warm-start inside the run (previous theta used as init for ML-II)
#
# Output:
#   Prints batch best, best_overall, mark_score progression (batches 3-15 only)
#   At end prints best and mark_score for that run.
#
# Notes:
#   - You can set N_RUNS=5 for "professor evaluation style", or larger for your own testing.
#   - This does NOT hardcode any specific basin locations from past runs. Bias is only via
#     the init distribution + candidate densification around *within-run* best.
# =============================================================

